## Avatar Script

[INTRO - 0:00-0:25]
"Your Dashboard should reflect what matters most to you and your role. In this video, I'll show you how to customize the Dashboard layout, choose which widgets to display, and set up your personalized transformation command center. This feature is available on Pro and Enterprise plans."

[SECTION 1: Entering Edit Mode - 0:25-1:00]
"To start customizing, look for the 'Customize' button in the top right corner of your Dashboard. Clicking it enters edit mode – you'll notice the interface changes slightly, with handles appearing on each widget.

In edit mode, you can move widgets around, resize them, and access widget settings. Take a moment to look at the current layout and think about what you'd like to change."

[SECTION 2: Moving and Resizing Widgets - 1:00-2:00]
"Moving widgets is as simple as drag and drop. Click and hold the header of any widget, then drag it to your preferred position. The other widgets will automatically rearrange to make room.

To resize a widget, grab the handle in the bottom-right corner and drag. Some widgets work better when larger – for example, the Activity Feed benefits from more vertical space, while the Maturity Score looks great in a compact square format.

As you experiment, you'll see a grid overlay helping you align widgets neatly. The system prevents overlaps, so everything stays organized."

[SECTION 3: Widget Settings - 2:00-2:45]
"Each widget has a settings gear icon that appears in edit mode. Click it to access widget-specific options.

For the Maturity Score widget, you can choose which assessment frameworks to include in the calculation, and whether to show the trend indicator.

The Initiative widget lets you filter by status – maybe you only want to see at-risk items on your Dashboard. The Activity Feed can be filtered by activity type or team members.

These settings let you focus on what's most relevant to your daily work."

[SECTION 4: Adding and Removing Widgets - 2:45-3:30]
"Want to add a new widget? Click the 'Add Widget' button to see all available options. You might add a KPI tracker, a team performance summary, or an upcoming milestones widget.

Select a widget from the catalog, choose its initial size, and it'll be added to your Dashboard. You can then position it wherever you like.

To remove a widget, click the X icon that appears in edit mode. Don't worry – removing a widget doesn't delete any data, and you can always add it back later."

[SECTION 5: Saving Your Layout - 3:30-4:00]
"When you're happy with your customized Dashboard, click 'Save Layout' to preserve your changes. Your customization is tied to your user account, so it'll be there whenever you log in, from any device.

If you ever want to start fresh, there's a 'Reset to Default' option that restores the original Dashboard layout."

[OUTRO - 4:00-4:30]
"A well-customized Dashboard helps you work more efficiently by surfacing the information you need most. Spend a few minutes setting it up now, and you'll save time every day.

You're now a Dashboard power user! Next up, we'll dive into the Assessment module – the foundation of your transformation journey. Let's go!"

